  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrating upSCALE into the Ministry of Health [Mozambique]</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">upSCALE is an electronic community health information system (eCHIS). The eCHIS software is uploaded onto a mobile phone and provided to the community health workers known locally as Agentes polivalentes de sa&#xfa;de (APSs). It is designed to improve quality of care and enhance reporting rates to improve data for decision making.

The project started in 2016 as a pilot and has since scaled up. This current UNICEF grant started in January 2025 with the aim of institutionalising upSCALE into the Ministry of Health through data ownership and data-informed decision-making for the community health programme.

Through this grant, upSCALE will be scaled up to all 10 provinces covering all districts in each province and equipping every APS with a digital device.
[Mozambique]</narrative>
  </description>
